<title>USA: Weekend Box Office Chart - September 20-22.</title>
<headline>Weekend Box Office Chart - September 20-22.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are final data for the top 10 movies at the September 20-22 weekend box office, according to Exhibitor Relations Co. Inc.</p>
<p>    Film		    Three-Day Gross     Cumulative Gross</p>
<p>1. First Wives Club	 $18,913,411	 $ ------</p>
<p>2. Last Man Standing	$ 7,010,333	 $ ------</p>
<p>3. Fly Away Home	    $ 3,833,514	 $  9,505,591</p>
<p>4. Maximum Risk	     $ 2,908,156	 $ 10,273,400</p>
<p>5. Bulletproof		$ 2,615,855	 $ 15,624,765</p>
<p>6. First Kid		  $ 2,322,797	 $ 20,193,336</p>
<p>7. Tin Cup		    $ 1,803,879	 $ 49,471,647</p>
<p>8. A Time To Kill	   $ 1,601,518	 $103,308,837</p>
<p>9. Independence Day	 $ 1,591,751	 $290,605,002</p>
<p>10 The Rich Man's Wife    $ 1,571,989	 $  5,616,889</p>
<p>NOTE: First Wives Club is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc. &quot;Last Man Standing&quot; is released by New Line Cinema, a unit of Turner Broadcasting System Inc. &quot;Fly Away Home&quot; and &quot;Maximum Risk&quot; are released by Columbia Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp. &quot;Bulletproof&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd.. &quot;First Kid&quot; and &quot;The Rich Man's Wife&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co.. &quot;Tin Cup&quot; and &quot;A Time To Kill&quot; are released by Time Warner Inc.'s Warner Bros.</p>
<p>&quot;Independence Day&quot; is released by News Corp.'s 20th Century Fox.</p>
<p>Reuters/Variety</p>
